cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below. If you cite a measured figure, cite the commit and the split it came from."
title: "Project SHARDEX: Mirror a codebase, shatter it into content-addressed shards, forge a shard into a FLAME arena."
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: CDDL-1.1
type: software
abstract: >-
  SHARDEX mirrors a codebase, shatters it into content-addressed shards,
  and forges a shard into a FLAME arena. The pipeline runs on the Python
  standard library: mirror, shatter, forge, tune, and verify rungs
  (`shardex.py`, `ops.py`, `meshscene.py`, `transubstantiate.py`) with the
  forged `flame.html` shell running on the browser's own JavaScript with no
  external script, font, or stylesheet reference.
authors:
  - name: "Project SHARDEX contributors"
keywords:
  - code mirroring
  - content-addressed shards
  - game engine
  - transubstantiation
  - FLAME engine
  - open source
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Project FLAME"
    notes: "Target engine for forged shards."
    url: "https://github.com/myzticalbabe/azazael/tree/main/Project_FLAME"
  - type: software
    title: "Project FLAMING SWORD"
    notes: "Code quality sweep used in the pipeline."
    url: "https://github.com/myzticalbabe/azazael/tree/main/Project_FLAMING_SWORD"